            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method performed by a user equipment, UE, in a wireless communication system, the method comprising transmitting, to a base station, UE capability information indicating that the UE supports physical uplink control channel, PUCCH, repetitions related to multiple transmission and reception points, TRPs; receiving, from the base station, a medium access control, MAC, control element, CE, associated with a PUCCH spatial relation activation for the PUCCH repetitions, the MAC CE including a first PUCCH spatial relation information identifier, ID, a second PUCCH spatial relation information ID and a PUCCH resource ID which is to be activated with first spatial relation information and second spatial relation information, wherein the MAC CE is applied to all PUCCH resources in a PUCCH resource group including the PUCCH resource ID; and performing a PUCCH transmission associated with the PUCCH repetitions, wherein the first spatial relation information and the second spatial relation information are used for the PUCCH repetitions, based on information associated with a transmission order and configured by a higher layer signaling</p>
            </abstract>
